Current GetSignal/GetAll behavior in HybridLiveSignalStore (the bug being fixed):

1. GetAll(LiveSignalReadDistributed) (live_store.go:199-219)
   - Calls l2.GetAllValues; on err returns err.
   - If raw map is empty, falls through to L1 GetAll.
   - Otherwise returns freshSignalValues(values, s.now()) — which DROPS every
     legacy scalar (Timestamp.IsZero()) and every entry older than
     LiveSignalFreshnessThreshold (2 minutes).
   - L1 is NEVER consulted when L2 returns ANY entry, even if every entry
     gets stripped by the freshness filter. This is failure (a) in
     phase-38-00 and matches the dashboard zero-values bug.

2. GetSignal(LiveSignalReadDistributed) (live_store.go:170-196)
   - Calls l2.GetSignalValue; on err returns err.
   - If IsLiveSignalFresh -> returns the L2 value.
   - If value != nil but stale -> returns (nil, nil) without trying L1.
   - If value == nil -> falls through to L1.
   This drops stale L2 values and never merges with L1 even when L1 has
   a fresher local snapshot from the telemetry hot path.

3. LiveSignalReadLocal (both methods)
   - Always reads L1 via cloneSignalValue/cloneSignalValues. Never touches
     Redis. This is the correct hot-path behavior and must be preserved.

4. IsLiveSignalFresh (redis_cache.go:111-122)
   - nil value -> false.
   - Zero Timestamp -> false (legacy unknown freshness).
   - age > LiveSignalFreshnessThreshold (2m) -> false.
   - Otherwise true. This is contract-correct and must be preserved.

