  ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  T1. TestHybridLiveSignalStoreGetAllReturnsL2OnlyAndL1OnlySignalsTogether
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Rule: R1 (UNION of L1 and L2 in distributed reads).
  Setup:
    - local := New()
    - local.Update(vehicleID, {"L1Only": "from_l1"})  // L1-only signal
    - redisCache.Update(ctx, vehicleID, {"L2Only": 12.5}) // L2-only signal,
        timestamped envelope inside the freshness window
    - liveStore mode = hybrid
  Action: values, err := liveStore.GetAll(ctx, vehicleID, LiveSignalReadDistributed)
  Assertions:
    - err is nil
    - values["L1Only"].Raw == "from_l1"
    - values["L2Only"].Raw == 12.5
    - len(values) >= 2 (no other signals required)
  Why this fails today: GetAll returns only the L2 freshSignalValues map
  when L2 returns any entries; "L1Only" is dropped.

  ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  T2. TestHybridLiveSignalStoreGetAllReturnsLegacyScalarL2Values
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Rule: R2 (LEGACY_SCALAR_RETAINED — legacy scalar values returned, never
  silently dropped, with zero Timestamp preserved so freshness is unknown).
  Setup:
    - local := New() (empty)
    - redisClient.hashes[redisSignalKey(vehicleID)] = {
        "legacy_speed": "88.5",
        "legacy_state": "asleep",
      }   // raw scalar bytes, no envelope -> Timestamp.IsZero() on decode
    - liveStore mode = hybrid
  Action: values, err := liveStore.GetAll(ctx, vehicleID, LiveSignalReadDistributed)
  Assertions:
    - err is nil
    - values["legacy_speed"].Raw == 88.5
    - values["legacy_state"].Raw == "asleep"
    - values["legacy_speed"].Timestamp.IsZero() is true
    - values["legacy_state"].Timestamp.IsZero() is true
    - IsLiveSignalFresh(values["legacy_speed"], time.Now().UTC()) is false
    - IsLiveSignalFresh(values["legacy_state"], time.Now().UTC()) is false
  Why this fails today: freshSignalValues drops zero-Timestamp entries,
  so values is empty (or only contains an L1 fallback if L2 was empty).

  ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  T3. TestHybridLiveSignalStoreGetAllReturnsStaleL2EnvelopesWithTimestampPreserved
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Rule: R3 (STALE_ENVELOPE_RETAINED — stale envelope values returned,
  never silently dropped, with their original Timestamp preserved so
  IsLiveSignalFresh remains the freshness oracle).
  Setup:
    - local := New() (empty)
    - Build a timestamped envelope manually (or via redisCache.Update with
      an injected clock) so the envelope's Timestamp is
      `now - LiveSignalFreshnessThreshold - 5*time.Minute` (well outside
      the 2m freshness window).
    - Insert it into redisClient.hashes[redisSignalKey(vehicleID)] under
      field "Odometer".
    - liveStore mode = hybrid; pin liveStore.now = func() time.Time { return now }
  Action: values, err := liveStore.GetAll(ctx, vehicleID, LiveSignalReadDistributed)
  Assertions:
    - err is nil
    - values["Odometer"] is not nil
    - values["Odometer"].Raw equals the encoded numeric value
    - values["Odometer"].Timestamp equals the original stale timestamp
      (i.e. the timestamp is preserved verbatim, not zeroed and not
      restamped)
    - IsLiveSignalFresh(values["Odometer"], now) is false
  Why this fails today: freshSignalValues drops any entry with age
  greater than LiveSignalFreshnessThreshold; values would be empty
  (or only contain an L1 fallback when L2 is otherwise empty).

  ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  T4. TestHybridLiveSignalStoreGetAllMergesL1AndL2WithNewerTimestampWinning
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Rule: R4 (L1_L2_MERGE_RULE — newer non-zero Timestamp wins; legacy
  loses to any timestamped value; L2 wins ties on identical non-zero
  Timestamps).
  Setup:
